<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  robot: arm_snapshot_preview | consumer: generic URDF geometry/kinematics review
  status: PREVIEW, NOT CONTROL-READY OR DYNAMICS-READY
  units: meters, kilograms, seconds, radians; all STL coordinates are meters
  source: isolated CAD copy in ../cad; original component transforms and six
    top-level RefAxis features in ../planning/assembly_snapshot.json
  zero pose: original snapshot explicitly confirmed by the user; do NOT replace
    it with the re-solved CAD pose, which shifts the wrist by about 20.23 mm
  root: base_link at original CAD origin; robot +X=-CAD Z, +Y=-CAD X, +Z=CAD Y
    This is a documented coordinate convention, not a surveyed mounting datum.
  link frames: link1 through link6 coincide with joint1 through joint6 at zero.
    Each origin is the closest point on its frozen CAD axis to the previous
    frame origin; these mathematical origins are not claimed flange centers.
    Frame Z follows the CAD axis endpoint order; X projects robot forward onto
    its normal plane, falling back to robot left; Y completes the right-hand frame.
  positive motion: right-hand rotation about each local +Z; CAD endpoint order
    is provisional and has NOT been checked against motor/encoder conventions.
  meshes: ../meshes/urdf/visual and ../meshes/urdf/collision; geometry in owning link frames,
    identity geometry origins, explicit scale 1 1 1; colors are review labels.
  membership: ../derived/link_membership.json; 180 displayed part instances,
    two originally hidden instances retained only in the raw geometry cache,
    12 suppressed instances excluded. Hidden solid/surface helper bodies are
    filtered using native body visibility. Every active instance is accounted for.
  boundary assumptions: structural subassemblies seed the links; J5 inner shaft
    and driven pulley are assigned to link5, J6 large output pulley to link6,
    and the loose screw to link3 using recorded mate evidence. Physical boundary
    and motion review remains required; internal transmission motion is simplified.
  inertials: populated for all seven physical links from native SolidWorks
    IMassProperty2 effective link selections after native deletion/keep-body
    removal of hidden spherical bodies 旋转1/旋转2/旋转3. Properties use
    IncludeHiddenBodiesOrComponents=false, matching the exported visible-body
    policy; assembly mass overrides are retained. Values are CAD-derived and
    still require hardware material/encoder calibration before control use.
  collision: compound component convex hulls, a conservative preview model;
    platform-specific collision decomposition and interference review are pending.
  limits: ALL lower/upper/velocity/effort values are deliberate zero placeholders.
    They lock this preview to its zero pose, are NOT actual hardware parameters,
    and MUST be replaced before controller use or full-range motion verification.
    Do not infer unlimited rotation or change these joints to continuous.
  tool0: frame-only identity alias of link6, not a calibrated TCP; no mass/geometry.
  gripper: held at the original opening and merged into link6; no gripper joints.
  canonical artifact: edit this XML directly; helper scripts compute and verify
    geometry/frames only, and do not regenerate this URDF.
-->
